Subject: Compile functions unused in a build out of it

What this does
  Narrows the guards on functions that have no caller in a given
  configuration: regvm_frame_alloc, regvm_frame_release and
  regvm_inloop_eligible to `#if QJS_REGVM_INLOOP_CALL`; regvm_writer_atom,
  regvm_reader_atom and regvm_validate_code to `#if QJS_AOT`;
  regvm_t_get_field_chain_free1 to `#if !QJS_DRC`; and js_scan_argv_safe to
  `#if !QJS_REGVM || QJS_AOT`.

Why we need it
  Each is compiled in a build where its only caller is absent, so it is a
  -Wunused-function warning there. The guards match the call sites exactly, so
  no build loses a function it uses.

What it adds
  Guards only. No function is added, renamed or changed.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.

